# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ProblemSolver — environment variables
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in real values for local development.
# NEVER commit ".env" or put real secrets in source code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Database (PostgreSQL via Neon / Supabase free tier during development) ---
# Pooled connection string used by the app at runtime.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/problemsolver?sslmode=require"

# Direct (non-pooled) connection string used by Prisma Migrate.
# On Neon this is the same host without "-pooler"; on Supabase it is the
# same URL with the direct/session port. If your provider only gives you
# one URL, set DIRECT_URL to the same value as DATABASE_URL.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/problemsolver?sslmode=require"

# --- Site configuration ---
# Public base URL, used for canonical links, sitemap.xml, robots.txt and
# OpenGraph metadata. No trailing slash.
# IMPORTANT: getSiteUrl() (src/lib/utils.ts) falls back to
# "http://localhost:3000" if this isn't set. If you deploy without setting
# this to your real production domain, every canonical URL, sitemap entry,
# and Open Graph tag will silently emit localhost URLs in production —
# this is exactly the class of bug that causes Google to index the wrong
# domain or reject pages for a mismatched canonical. Set this in your
# hosting provider's environment variables (e.g. Vercel project settings),
# not just in a local .env file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Analytics (privacy-conscious, cookie-free product analytics) ---
# Phase 1 ships the event-tracking architecture only (see
# src/lib/analytics/events.ts); no analytics provider is wired in yet.
# When you enable one in a later phase (e.g. Plausible or Umami, both of
# which are free/low-cost and do not use cookies), set these:
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=""

# --- Admin (used starting Phase 9 — present now so the shape is known) ---
# Long random string used to sign the admin session cookie. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=""

# --- AI tools (used starting Phase 5 — not required for Phase 1) ---
# Left blank on purpose. Do not add a paid API key until the AI phase.
AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=""

# --- Runtime ---
NODE_ENV="development"
